# Zaza — Cursor project rules
# Goal: Always load the concise seed (CLAUDE_SEED.md) for brand, safety, and tone.
# If deeper context is needed, consult CLAUDE.md. Default to teacher-first, safe, UK English.

[CONTEXT]
- Read ./CLAUDE_SEED.md at the start of each session or task.
- If the task involves product positioning, copy, or UX, also skim ./CLAUDE.md.

[STYLE]
- UK English; no em dashes (use hyphens).
- Plain, supportive, teacher-first tone.
- Accessibility- and bias-aware by default.

[GUARDRAILS]
- Hallucination-safe patterns; provide short "why this" hints when helpful.
- Privacy-first; do not invent schools, data, or claims.

[PRODUCT SCOPE]
- Zaza suite: Teach, Draft, GradeFlow, Shield; all powered by KnowledgeCore platform.
- Keep messaging aligned with CLAUDE_SEED.md product blurbs and trust signals.

[WHEN CODING]
- Keep dependencies minimal.
- If adding new deps or changing build/CI/auth, open ADR + PR explaining trade-offs.
- Add i18n keys (EN/DE) for any user-facing strings.

[WHEN WRITING COPY]
- Start from CLAUDE_SEED.md positioning.
- Keep copy concise, professional, and parent-ready.
- Prefer explainable outputs and safe defaults.

[ESCALATION]
- When unsure about policy/safety/positioning, quote the relevant line from CLAUDE_SEED.md or CLAUDE.md and ask for confirmation.
